course: dictionary
lesson: 5133
title: Investigator
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An investigator is a person whose job is to find out the facts about something, such as a crime or an accident. They ask questions and look for evidence, which means things that help show what really happened.
explain: «If something ever goes wrong in the air, two tough recorders called the black box help investigators find out why, so that it never happens again.» The words find out why tell you that an investigator looks for the reason something happened.
explain: Context can also show which kind of investigator is meant. A private investigator is paid by people, not by the police. A crime scene investigator works at the place where a crime happened. The words around the word tell you which one.
explain: In science, you become an investigator too. You ask a question, plan a fair test, collect evidence and draw conclusions from what you found.
fact: An investigator finds out the facts about something, such as a crime or an accident.
fact: A private investigator is a detective who is paid by people, not by the police.
fact: In science, an investigator is a researcher who carries out a study.
fact: Investigators look at the causes of accidents, such as air crash investigators who find out why a plane went wrong.
fact: «Investigators» is the plural, which means more than one investigator.
exercise: «If something ever goes wrong in the air, two tough recorders called the black box help investigators find out why.» What are investigators trying to find out? | How many people flew on the plane | What colour the box is | *Why something happened | How to build a new aeroplane
exercise: Leo says a private investigator must work for the police. Is he right? | Yes, private means the police are secret | No, a private investigator is a scientist in a lab | *No, a private investigator is paid by people, not by the police | Yes, every investigator works for the police
exercise: In science, what does an investigator do? | Sleeps in a laboratory all day | Wins prizes for drawing | Only reads stories about mysteries | *Carries out a study to find answers
test: What is evidence? | A prize for the best answer | A type of weather | A kind of cloth used for curtains | *Facts or things that help show what really happened
test: In science, what is an investigator? | A teacher who marks tests | A person who writes news stories only | A police officer on a motorbike | *A researcher who carries out a study
exam: «If something ever goes wrong in the air, two tough recorders called the black box help investigators find out why.» What does investigators mean here? | *People whose job is to find out why something happened | Pilots who fly planes | Boxes that record sounds | People who sell tickets
